{"pageProps": {"params": {"versionId": "59", "usfm": "1CH.1.NIV"}, "audioVersionInfo": {"title": "ESV Hear the Word Audio Bible", "copyright_long": {"text": "English: ESV Audio Old and New Testament", "html": "English: ESV Audio Old and New Testament"}, "copyright_short": {"text": "\u2117 2016 Crossway", "html": "<p>\u2117 2016 Crossway</p>"}, "version_id": 59, "id": 1, "publisher_link": "", "dramatized": false, "publisher": {"id": 575, "name": "Hear Book Audio", "local_name": "Hear Book Audio", "url": null, "description": null}}, "type": "chapter", "chapterInfo": {"audioChapterInfo": [{"download_urls": {"format_mp3_32k": "//audio-bible-cdn.youversionapi.com/1/32k/1CH/1-fab59dd409790a6c500bff18a41c3142.mp3?version_id=59", "format_hls": "//audio-hls.youversionapi.com/1/m4a/32k/1CH/1-fab59dd409790a6c500bff18a41c3142.m3u8?version_id=59"}, "id": 1, "version_id": 59, "title": "ESV Hear the Word Audio Bible", "timing_available": true, "dramatized": false, "default": true}], "content": "<div class=\"version vid59 iso6393eng\" data-vid=\"59\" data-iso6393=\"eng\">\n    <div class=\"book bk1CH\">\n        <div class=\"chapter ch1\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1\">\n            <div class=\"label\">1</div><div class=\"s1\"><span class=\"heading\">From Adam to Abraham</span></div><div class=\"p\"><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"verse v1\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.1\"><span class=\"label\">1</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note f\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\"><span class=\"ft\">  </span><span class=\"fr\">1:1 </span><span class=\"ft\">  </span><span class=\"ft\">Many names in these genealogies are spelled differently in other biblical books</span><span class=\"ft\">  </span></span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Gen. 4:25, 26; 5:3, 6</span></span><span class=\"content\">Adam, Seth, Enosh; </span></span><span class=\"verse v2\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.2\"><span class=\"label\">2</span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">For ver. 2-4, see Gen. 5:9-32</span></span><span class=\"content\">Kenan, Mahalalel, Jared; </span></span><span class=\"verse v3\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.3\"><span class=\"label\">3</span><span class=\"content\">Enoch, Methuselah, Lamech; </span></span><span class=\"verse v4\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.4\"><span class=\"label\">4</span><span class=\"content\">Noah, </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Gen. 6:10; 9:18</span></span><span class=\"content\">Shem, Ham, and Japheth.</span></span></div><div class=\"p\"><span class=\"verse v4\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.4\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v5\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.5\"><span class=\"label\">5</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    For ver. 5-7, see Gen. 10:2-4  </span></span><span class=\"content\">The sons of Japheth: Gomer, Magog, Madai, Javan, Tubal, Meshech, and Tiras. </span></span><span class=\"verse v6\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.6\"><span class=\"label\">6</span><span class=\"content\">The sons of Gomer: Ashkenaz, Riphath,</span><span class=\"note f\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\"><span class=\"fr\">1:6 </span><span class=\"ft\">Septuagint; Hebrew </span><span class=\"fq\">Diphath</span></span></span><span class=\"content\"> and Togarmah. </span></span><span class=\"verse v7\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.7\"><span class=\"label\">7</span><span class=\"content\">The sons of Javan: Elishah, Tarshish, Kittim, and Rodanim.</span></span></div><div class=\"p\"><span class=\"verse v7\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.7\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v8\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.8\"><span class=\"label\">8</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    For ver. 8-10, see Gen. 10:6-8  </span></span><span class=\"content\">The sons of Ham: Cush, Egypt, Put, and Canaan. </span></span><span class=\"verse v9\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.9\"><span class=\"label\">9</span><span class=\"content\">The sons of Cush: Seba, Havilah, Sabta, Raamah, and Sabteca. The sons of Raamah: Sheba and Dedan. </span></span><span class=\"verse v10\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.10\"><span class=\"label\">10</span><span class=\"content\">Cush fathered Nimrod. He was the first on earth to be a mighty man.</span><span class=\"note f\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\"><span class=\"fr\">1:10 </span><span class=\"ft\">Or </span><span class=\"fq\">He began to be a mighty man on the earth</span></span></span></span></div><div class=\"p\"><span class=\"verse v10\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.10\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v11\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.11\"><span class=\"label\">11</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    For ver. 11-16, see Gen. 10:10-18  </span></span><span class=\"content\">Egypt fathered Ludim, Anamim, Lehabim, Naphtuhim, </span></span><span class=\"verse v12\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.12\"><span class=\"label\">12</span><span class=\"content\">Pathrusim, Casluhim (from whom the Philistines came), and Caphtorim.</span></span></div><div class=\"p\"><span class=\"verse v12\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.12\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v13\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.13\"><span class=\"label\">13</span><span class=\"content\">Canaan fathered Sidon his firstborn and Heth, </span></span><span class=\"verse v14\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.14\"><span class=\"label\">14</span><span class=\"content\">and the Jebusites, the Amorites, the Girgashites, </span></span><span class=\"verse v15\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.15\"><span class=\"label\">15</span><span class=\"content\">the Hivites, the Arkites, the Sinites, </span></span><span class=\"verse v16\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.16\"><span class=\"label\">16</span><span class=\"content\">the Arvadites, the Zemarites, and the Hamathites.</span></span></div><div class=\"p\"><span class=\"verse v16\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.16\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v17\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.17\"><span class=\"label\">17</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    For ver. 17-23, see Gen. 10:22-29  </span></span><span class=\"content\">The sons of Shem: Elam, Asshur, Arpachshad, Lud, and Aram. And the sons of Aram:</span><span class=\"note f\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\"><span class=\"fr\">1:17 </span><span class=\"ft\">Septuagint; Hebrew lacks </span><span class=\"fq\">And the sons of Aram</span></span></span><span class=\"content\"> Uz, Hul, Gether, and Meshech. </span></span><span class=\"verse v18\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.18\"><span class=\"label\">18</span><span class=\"content\">Arpachshad fathered Shelah, and Shelah fathered Eber. </span></span><span class=\"verse v19\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.19\"><span class=\"label\">19</span><span class=\"content\">To Eber were born two sons: the name of the one was Peleg</span><span class=\"note f\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\"><span class=\"fr\">1:19 </span><span class=\"fq\">Peleg </span><span class=\"ft\">means </span><span class=\"fq\">division</span></span></span><span class=\"content\"> (for in his days the earth was divided), and his brother&#8217;s name was Joktan. </span></span><span class=\"verse v20\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.20\"><span class=\"label\">20</span><span class=\"content\">Joktan fathered Almodad, Sheleph, Hazarmaveth, Jerah, </span></span><span class=\"verse v21\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.21\"><span class=\"label\">21</span><span class=\"content\">Hadoram, Uzal, Diklah, </span></span><span class=\"verse v22\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.22\"><span class=\"label\">22</span><span class=\"content\">Obal,</span><span class=\"note f\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\"><span class=\"fr\">1:22 </span><span class=\"ft\">Septuagint, Syriac (compare Genesis 10:28); Hebrew </span><span class=\"fq\">Ebal</span></span></span><span class=\"content\"> Abimael, Sheba, </span></span><span class=\"verse v23\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.23\"><span class=\"label\">23</span><span class=\"content\">Ophir, Havilah, and Jobab; all these were the sons of Joktan.</span></span></div><div class=\"p\"><span class=\"verse v23\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.23\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v24\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.24\"><span class=\"label\">24</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    For ver. 24, 27, see Gen. 11:10-26; Luke 3:34-36  </span></span><span class=\"content\">Shem, Arpachshad, Shelah; </span></span><span class=\"verse v25\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.25\"><span class=\"label\">25</span><span class=\"content\">Eber, Peleg, Reu; </span></span><span class=\"verse v26\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.26\"><span class=\"label\">26</span><span class=\"content\">Serug, Nahor, Terah; </span></span><span class=\"verse v27\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.27\"><span class=\"label\">27</span><span class=\"content\">Abram, that is, Abraham.</span></span></div><div class=\"s1\"><span class=\"heading\">From Abraham to Jacob</span></div><div class=\"p\"><span class=\"verse v27\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.27\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v28\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.28\"><span class=\"label\">28</span><span class=\"content\">The sons of Abraham: </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Gen. 21:2, 3 </span></span><span class=\"content\">Isaac and </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Gen. 16:11, 15</span></span><span class=\"content\">Ishmael. </span></span><span class=\"verse v29\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.29\"><span class=\"label\">29</span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">For ver. 29-31, see Gen. 25:13-16</span></span><span class=\"content\">These are their genealogies: the firstborn of Ishmael, Nebaioth, and Kedar, Adbeel, Mibsam, </span></span><span class=\"verse v30\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.30\"><span class=\"label\">30</span><span class=\"content\">Mishma, Dumah, Massa, Hadad, Tema, </span></span><span class=\"verse v31\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.31\"><span class=\"label\">31</span><span class=\"content\">Jetur, Naphish, and Kedemah. These are the sons of Ishmael. </span></span><span class=\"verse v32\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.32\"><span class=\"label\">32</span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">For ver. 32, 33, see Gen. 25:1-4</span></span><span class=\"content\">The sons of Keturah, Abraham&#8217;s concubine: she bore Zimran, Jokshan, Medan, Midian, Ishbak, and Shuah. The sons of Jokshan: Sheba and Dedan. </span></span><span class=\"verse v33\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.33\"><span class=\"label\">33</span><span class=\"content\">The sons of Midian: Ephah, Epher, Hanoch, Abida, and Eldaah. All these were the descendants of Keturah.</span></span></div><div class=\"p\"><span class=\"verse v33\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.33\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v34\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.34\"><span class=\"label\">34</span><span class=\"content\">Abraham fathered </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[See ver. 28 above] </span></span><span class=\"content\">Isaac. The sons of Isaac: </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Gen. 25:25, 26 </span></span><span class=\"content\">Esau and </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Gen. 32:28</span></span><span class=\"content\">Israel. </span></span><span class=\"verse v35\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.35\"><span class=\"label\">35</span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">For ver. 35-37, see Gen. 36:4, 5, 9-13</span></span><span class=\"content\">The sons of Esau: Eliphaz, Reuel, Jeush, Jalam, and Korah. </span></span><span class=\"verse v36\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.36\"><span class=\"label\">36</span><span class=\"content\">The sons of Eliphaz: Teman, Omar, Zepho, Gatam, Kenaz, and of Timna,</span><span class=\"note f\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\"><span class=\"fr\">1:36 </span><span class=\"ft\">Septuagint (compare Genesis 36:12); Hebrew lacks </span><span class=\"fq\">and of</span></span></span><span class=\"content\"> Amalek. </span></span><span class=\"verse v37\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.37\"><span class=\"label\">37</span><span class=\"content\">The sons of Reuel: Nahath, Zerah, Shammah, and Mizzah.</span></span></div><div class=\"p\"><span class=\"verse v37\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.37\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v38\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.38\"><span class=\"label\">38</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    For ver. 38-42, see Gen. 36:20-28  </span></span><span class=\"content\">The sons of Seir: Lotan, Shobal, Zibeon, Anah, Dishon, Ezer, and Dishan. </span></span><span class=\"verse v39\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.39\"><span class=\"label\">39</span><span class=\"content\">The sons of Lotan: Hori and Hemam;</span><span class=\"note f\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\"><span class=\"fr\">1:39 </span><span class=\"ft\">Septuagint (compare Genesis 36:22); Hebrew </span><span class=\"fq\">Homam</span></span></span><span class=\"content\"> and Lotan&#8217;s sister was Timna. </span></span><span class=\"verse v40\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.40\"><span class=\"label\">40</span><span class=\"content\">The sons of Shobal: Alvan,</span><span class=\"note f\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\"><span class=\"fr\">1:40 </span><span class=\"ft\">Septuagint (compare Genesis 36:23); Hebrew </span><span class=\"fq\">Alian</span></span></span><span class=\"content\"> Manahath, Ebal, Shepho,</span><span class=\"note f\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\"><span class=\"fr\">1:40 </span><span class=\"ft\">Septuagint (compare Genesis 36:23); Hebrew </span><span class=\"fq\">Shephi</span></span></span><span class=\"content\"> and Onam. The sons of Zibeon: Aiah and Anah. </span></span><span class=\"verse v41\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.41\"><span class=\"label\">41</span><span class=\"content\">The son</span><span class=\"note f\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\"><span class=\"fr\">1:41 </span><span class=\"ft\">Hebrew </span><span class=\"fq\">sons</span></span></span><span class=\"content\"> of Anah: Dishon. The sons of Dishon: Hemdan,</span><span class=\"note f\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\"><span class=\"fr\">1:41 </span><span class=\"ft\">Septuagint (compare Genesis 36:26); Hebrew </span><span class=\"fq\">Hamran</span></span></span><span class=\"content\"> Eshban, Ithran, and Cheran. </span></span><span class=\"verse v42\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.42\"><span class=\"label\">42</span><span class=\"content\">The sons of Ezer: Bilhan, Zaavan, and Akan.</span><span class=\"note f\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\"><span class=\"fr\">1:42 </span><span class=\"ft\">Septuagint (compare Genesis 36:27); Hebrew </span><span class=\"fq\">Jaakan</span></span></span><span class=\"content\"> The sons of Dishan: Uz and Aran.</span></span></div><div class=\"p\"><span class=\"verse v42\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.42\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v43\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.43\"><span class=\"label\">43</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    For ver. 43-54, see Gen. 36:31-43  </span></span><span class=\"content\">These are the kings who reigned in the land of Edom before any king reigned over the people of Israel: Bela the son of Beor, the name of his city being Dinhabah. </span></span><span class=\"verse v44\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.44\"><span class=\"label\">44</span><span class=\"content\">Bela died, and Jobab the son of Zerah of </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Isa. 34:6; 63:1</span></span><span class=\"content\">Bozrah reigned in his place. </span></span><span class=\"verse v45\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.45\"><span class=\"label\">45</span><span class=\"content\">Jobab died, and Husham of the land of the </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Gen. 36:11; Job 2:11; Jer. 49:7, 20; Ezek. 25:13</span></span><span class=\"content\">Temanites reigned in his place. </span></span><span class=\"verse v46\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.46\"><span class=\"label\">46</span><span class=\"content\">Husham died, and Hadad the son of Bedad, who defeated Midian in the country of Moab, reigned in his place, the name of his city being Avith. </span></span><span class=\"verse v47\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.47\"><span class=\"label\">47</span><span class=\"content\">Hadad died, and Samlah of Masrekah reigned in his place. </span></span><span class=\"verse v48\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.48\"><span class=\"label\">48</span><span class=\"content\">Samlah died, and Shaul of Rehoboth on the Euphrates</span><span class=\"note f\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\"><span class=\"fr\">1:48 </span><span class=\"ft\">Hebrew </span><span class=\"fq\">the River</span></span></span><span class=\"content\"> reigned in his place. </span></span><span class=\"verse v49\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.49\"><span class=\"label\">49</span><span class=\"content\">Shaul died, and Baal-hanan, the son of Achbor, reigned in his place. </span></span><span class=\"verse v50\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.50\"><span class=\"label\">50</span><span class=\"content\">Baal-hanan died, and Hadad reigned in his place, the name of his city being Pai; and his wife&#8217;s name was Mehetabel, the daughter of Matred, the daughter of Mezahab. </span></span><span class=\"verse v51\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.51\"><span class=\"label\">51</span><span class=\"content\">And Hadad died.</span></span></div><div class=\"p\"><span class=\"verse v51\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.51\"><span class=\"content\">The chiefs of Edom were: chiefs Timna, Alvah, Jetheth, </span></span><span class=\"verse v52\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.52\"><span class=\"label\">52</span><span class=\"content\">Oholibamah, Elah, Pinon, </span></span><span class=\"verse v53\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.53\"><span class=\"label\">53</span><span class=\"content\">Kenaz, Teman, Mibzar, </span></span><span class=\"verse v54\" data-usfm=\"1CH.1.54\"><span class=\"label\">54</span><span class=\"content\">Magdiel, and Iram; these are the chiefs of Edom.</span></span></div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n</div>", "copyright": {"html": "<p>The Holy Bible, English Standard Version\u00ae (ESV\u00ae), copyright \u00a9 2001 by Crossway, a publishing ministry of Good News Publishers.</p>", "text": "The Holy Bible, English Standard Version\u00ae (ESV\u00ae), copyright \u00a9 2001 by Crossway, a publishing ministry of Good News Publishers."}, "next": {"canonical": true, "usfm": ["1CH.2"], "human": "1 Chronicles 2", "toc": true, "version_id": 59}, "previous": {"canonical": true, "usfm": ["2KI.25"], "human": "2 Kings 25", "toc": true, "version_id": 59}, "reference": {"usfm": ["1CH.1"], "human": "1 Chronicles 1", "version_id": 59}}, "usfm": "1CH.1.NIV", "locale": "en", "versionData": {"audio": true, "copyright_short": {"html": "<p>The Holy Bible, English Standard Version\u00ae (ESV\u00ae), copyright \u00a9 2001 by Crossway, a publishing ministry of Good News Publishers.</p>", "text": "The Holy Bible, English Standard Version\u00ae (ESV\u00ae), copyright \u00a9 2001 by Crossway, a publishing ministry of Good News Publishers."}, "id": 59, "language": {"iso_639_1": "en", "iso_639_3": "eng", "language_tag": "eng", "local_name": "English", "text_direction": "ltr"